<h5 id="objects">Objects</h5>

<p>An object in Objective-C is a pointer to an <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">objc_object</code>, <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">typedef struct objc_object *id;</code> As can be seen from its struct, it contains an isa pointer that points to the class object of this object. An object instance finds its own Class through this isa, and this Class stores the instance’s method list, property list, ivar list, and other related information.</p>

